 "scheme": "none",
 "seed": 12,
 "model": "lora",
 "stop": "20 lines",
 "poem": "My mother is here, and mother,\nAnd many a lovely mother,\nHolds in her hand the babe she never\nGave to man or woman else before.\nShe holds it like this--her own baby!\nHer own child!  Her mother's baby!\nAs sweetly as any mother,\nThe fair infant that you behold!\nYou see how hands are folded\nAlike across her bosom wide,\nIn tender embrace the baby,\nWho waits for us by his mother.\nI will talk with her; and then again\nYour white marble faces appear,\nWith your warm arms enveloping me,\nLike creatures that have all they desire,\nOnce more I will meet again.\nThey were not yet my fathers before,\nBut I myself am father.\nThe first of them, an angel-born child",
